{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured and restart-verified MariaDB on node1. The inventory database, InnoDB items table, local least-privilege account, and root-only credential file are healthy and persistent.","actions_performed":["Installed MariaDB 10.11 and enabled mariadb.service.","Generated a 256-bit credential on node1 without exposing it.","Created inventory.items and inventory_app@localhost with SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE privileges only.","Stored connection settings in /etc/inventory-db.env as root:root mode 0600.","Restarted node1 once, confirmed its boot ID changed, and verified service, schema, credentials, and test data recovered.","Removed the temporary restart-persistence probe row."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"MariaDB installed, enabled, and healthy","command_ids":["cmd-7afe8efee07b4f25","cmd-1b44c2a089ca4607","cmd-b6ef023a533d4eb9"],"summary":"Package installation succeeded; mariadb.service is enabled and active after restart."},{"requirement":"inventory database and items table","command_ids":["cmd-7d7a045b53584601","cmd-b6ef023a533d4eb9"],"summary":"Authenticated queries selected inventory and directly displayed the items table schema and InnoDB metadata."},{"requirement":"Local application account with appropriate access","command_ids":["cmd-7d7a045b53584601","cmd-b6ef023a533d4eb9"],"summary":"inventory_app authenticated as inventory_app@localhost; current grants are SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE on inventory only."},{"requirement":"Generated credential stored with root-only access","command_ids":["cmd-55a185d6fe2942cf","cmd-7d7a045b53584601","cmd-b6ef023a533d4eb9"],"summary":"Credential generation and configuration succeeded; /etc/inventory-db.env is a root:root regular file with mode 0600, and its stored credential successfully authenticates without being displayed."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-9b244ab81bd84d92","cmd-f02b787585454b8e","cmd-4c2d912571c14188","cmd-adf447dd6787490